AB  - Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipelines are now part of the new software delivery reality but due to their growing size, complexity, and heterogeneity, they create serious problems in terms of system reliability, security, and operational stability. The current CI/CD platforms are largely based on reactive monitoring and ruledriven mechanisms, which do not excel at detecting failures, performance breakdowns, and cascading failures of dynamic cloud-native systems. To overcome these shortcomings, this paper puts forward a RASEF-ML (Resilience-Aware Software Engineering Framework with Machine Learning), which is an allencompassing framework used to actively achieve software system resilience throughout the lifecycle. RASEF-ML framework uses machine learning models that are trained on both historical and real-time data of pipelines to determine the probability of failures, system stability, recoverability, and resilience in the whole system. Extensive experimental testing shows that the RASEF-ML framework performs much better than the state-of-the-art structures, such as the Production Environment Analyzer Framework and Adaptive DevSecOps frameworks, regarding the accuracy of failure forecasting, service failure reduction, recovery time, and resilience measure. The findings support the hypothesis that integrating machine learning-based resilience intelligence into software engineering systems can allow proactive risk mitigation and accelerated recovery in CI/CD-powered software systems as well as operational resiliency.
