AB  - The increasing integration of artificial intelligence into enterprise and industrial environments has heightened the operational complexity of maintaining machine learning (ML) models in production. Automated Model Lifecycle Management (AMLM) provides a unified and systematic approach to standardizing model operations across all lifecycle phases—ranging from data versioning and experimentation to deployment, continuous monitoring, and governance. Traditional manual workflows often introduce versioning conflicts, reproducibility issues, and delayed responses to model degradation. AMLM mitigates these challenges through a fully automated and auditable pipeline that combines continuous integration and deployment (CI/CD), experiment tracking, model packaging, automated drift detection, and governed model updates within a single framework.The proposed AMLM architecture integrates open-source ecosystems such as MLflow for model registry and TFX/Kubeflow-inspired pipelines for orchestrating production workflows. Central to the system is a modular policy engine that governs promotion, rollback, and retraining decisions while ensuring adherence to fairness, performance, and privacy constraints. A reproducible evaluation setup and a benchmark experiment under synthetic data drift scenarios demonstrate measurable improvements in operational resilience, deployment latency, and recovery efficiency.Beyond technical automation, AMLM fosters transparency, accountability, and compliance by embedding governance checkpoints and privacy-preserving mechanisms throughout the workflow. The framework serves as a practical blueprint for organizations aiming to reduce time-to-production, minimize failure risks, and enhance the reliability of AI-enabled operations.
ER  - 

