AB  - Modern development teams work in the business environments that has demanded a rapid delivery without the reduction of reliability. This study has recognized that the amount of source code is produced in the medium-to-large organizations has increased at a rate that manual inspection can no longer match. The developers often become overwhelmed by the volume of the required reviews. The core problem lies in defect introduction during a rapid iteration, uneven code review effectiveness, and an inefficient CI/CD execution that delay production releases. These challenges has indicated the need for an intelligent automation in the software engineering workflows. The proposed methodology has established an adaptive software pipeline that is powered by machine learning-enabled code intelligence. A hybrid embedding algorithm has combined the token-level semantic vectors with the graph-based structural embeddings in order to improve the representation of the source code artifacts. This improved representation has supported a multi-stage predictive system that includes an attention-based fault predictor to identify a higher-risk code segments prior to the combination. Here a suggestion generator has recommends the style and the functional corrections from the learned code patterns, and a reward-driven orchestration agent. This adjusts the CI/CD scheduling, test prioritization, and resource allocation based on real-time project conditions. The pipeline functions continuously during development, which allows autonomous refinement over time. The results has shown that the fault prediction module has achieved 95% accuracy, 94% precision, and 93% recall, which tends to reduce the post-release defects by 36% across benchmark datasets. The suggestion generator decreases the debugging time by 41%, and the adaptive CI/CD controller lowers testing and deployment latency by 32% while it maintains the operational stability. The system increases an overall developer productivity by 27%, which is evaluated using the validated effort-tracking indicators.
ER  - 

