AB  - This paper presents a practical and improved framework for automating the ASIC design flow using Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) through Jenkins. Unlike the usual manual or semi-automated design processes, this system adds a Machine Learning (ML)based model that uses the K-Means algorithm to create smart and flexible multi-corner SDC (Synopsys Design Constraint) files. Through the Jenkins interface, users can give basic inputs such as the technology node, RTL file, effort level, and an SDC template. Based on these inputs, the system automatically generates three constraint files - user, lighter, and tighter - which cover fast, typical, and slow process corners. Each part of the ASIC design flow, such as synthesis, floorplanning, placement, clock tree synthesis (CTS), routing, and GDSII generation, is built as a separate Jenkins job.Each stage of the ASIC flow is linked in sequence so that one process begins only after the earlier one completes properly. In addition, the flow can run on multiple servers at the same time, which helps to finish the overall design faster. At the end of the flow, KPI (Key Performance Indicator) plots of all the three key metrics that are area, power and timing are automatically generated. This system helps in reducing the design time, improving efficiency by catching the bugs early. Overall, this framework provides a simple, reliable and efficient CI/CD based methodology for modern ASIC design.
ER  - 

