AB  - Fast-moving cloud computing developments combined with DevOps practices created an urgent need for intelligent automation systems which boost application deployment as well as monitoring and management operations. Traditional DevOps workflows encounter difficulties when trying to scale their operations alongside efficiency and real-time adaptability within complex cloud environments. This research investigates how artificial intelligence systems advance DevOps automation through machine learning technology combined with predictive analytics and intelligent orchestration to boost cloud-native deployment pipelines. Organizations achieve automation of testing processes and infrastructure deployment and performance optimization through CI/CD systems powered by AI that require minimal human input. AI-based monitoring tools enable autonomous repairs of systems while simultaneously preventing security threats and performance-related failures in real time. AI technology enables automatic resource distribution and cost optimization which produces both speedier software deployments and enhanced business operational performance. Three essential artificial intelligence methodologies are deployed through the project: reinforcement learning for implementation planning and anomaly detection in log assessment and predictive analysis for system execution performance monitoring.
