AB  - Modern software systems increasingly rely on DevOps practices to enable rapid and reliable software delivery. However, traditional CI/CD pipelines and monitoring systems often lack adaptability to dynamic workloads and evolving system behavior. This paper presents an intelligent DevOps framework that integrates machine learning with Java-based micro services, cloud-native platforms, and automated CI/CD pipelines. The proposed system leverages ML models for anomaly detection, predictive analytics, and resource optimization, enhancing system reliability and operational efficiency. The architecture incorporates tools such as Jenkins, Kubernetes, and Prometheus, deployed on cloud platforms including AWS. Experimental evaluation demonstrates improvements in deployment efficiency, anomaly detection accuracy, and resource utilization. The results highlight the effectiveness of integrating AI-driven intelligence into DevOps workflows for nextgeneration cloud-based systems.
