AB  - Large-scale software development requires scalable CI/CD systems capable of executing complex distributed workflows. In practice, static and expert-defined resource configurations often lead to overestimation of CPU and system memory requirements, driving up operational costs. To address this, we introduce an intelligent orchestrator service within the SAP HANA CI system. Using historical execution data and machine learning, the system proactively predicts workload resource demands and dynamically adjusts resource allocations prior to task placement. The orchestrator adopts a plugin-based architecture in which a dedicated prediction strategy is assigned to each workload type. We demonstrate an implementation that successfully reduces memory over-provisioning in SAP HANA CI workloads.
ER  - 

