AB  - In rapid development cycles driven by Agile, web testing has become more and more important in guaranteeing software dependability and user satisfaction. A popular open-source automation tool for facilitating user interface testing in business settings is Selenium WebDriver. However, creating and maintaining reliable WebDriver test scripts often presents substantial organizational, process, and technical difficulties. The life cycle of creating WebDriver UI test scripts is thoroughly examined in this paper, along with the related frameworks, tools, and integration techniques in enterprise CI/CD pipelines. This paper also explores how scalability and stability concerns affect the efficacy of UI testing in enterprise Agile environments. This work presents empirical results from a financial case study and identifies persistent issues with the scalability and stability of test scripts. We also assess how Artificial Intelligence (AI) can be beneficial in creating and maintaining test scripts and other future scopes of AI in software testing. We emphasize the importance of organized frameworks, committed quality control procedures, and intelligent automation.
ER  - 

