AB  - The increasing complexity of web applications has increased the potential for security vulnerabilities because of the fast development cycles and insufficient implementation of security coding. Traditional Secure Development Lifecycles (SDKs) often do not find the proper balance between being agile while also being secure, which can result in an extended time to address a threat and more exposure. This thesis presents a new Intelligent Secure Development Lifecycle (ISDL) framework to fill the gap between software development and security enforcement by using Artificial Intelligence (AI) techniques. The framework incorporates the threat modeling, secure design synthesis, AI-augmented coding, automated test, infrastructure hardening and adaptive monitoring in the CI/CD pipeline. Experimental evaluation performed on two web application prototypes showed a 96.7% accuracy of detecting vulnerabilities, 3.8% false positive rate and 92.4% efficiency of the application remediation process, outperforming five well-established SDL methodologies. The results prove that the framework can deliver continuous, predictive and compliance-based security without jeopardizing the development velocity. The study concludes that intelligent driven automation across the phases of SDL leads to sustainable and adaptive-proactive defense mechanisms required for the security of the next generation of web applications.
ER  - 

